  "title": "Ziyarat of Imam Husayn (a.s.) — Karbala (All 6 General Forms)",
  "data": "First Ziyarah\nWhen you attend the sessions of the ruling authorities and mention the Imams, say:\nاَللَّهُمَّ أَرِنَا ٱلرَّخَاءَ وَٱلسُّرُورَ\nALLAAHUMMA ARENAR RAKHAAA-A WAS SOROORA\n‘O Allah, (please) show us luxury and pleasure.\nWhen you mention Imam al-Husayn (a.s.), repeat three times:\nصَلَّىٰ ٱللَّهُ عَلَيْكَ يَا أَبَا عَبْدِ ٱللَّهِ\nSALLAL LAAHO A’LAYKA YAA ABAA A’BDIL LAAHE\n‘May Allah bless you, O Abu-`Abdullah.’\nWhen you come to Abu-`Abdullah (al-Husayn), bathe yourself on the bank of the River Euphrates.\nPut on (ceremonially) pure clothes and walk barefooted, because you are in the sanctuary of Almighty Allah and His Messenger.\nUntil you stop at the gate of the shrine, repeat often: Allahu akbar, la ilaha illa Allah, subhan Allah, and Allahumma salli ala Muhammad wa ali Muhammad.\nAt the gate of the shrine, say:\nاَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَا حُجَّةَ ٱللَّهِ وَٱبْنَ حُجَّتِهِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA HUJJATAL LAAHE WABNA HUJJATEHI\nPeace be upon you, O Argument of Allah and son of His Argument.\nاَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكُمْ يَا مَلاَئِكَةَ ٱللَّهِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAYKUM YAA MALAAA-EKATAL LAAHE\nPeace be upon you all, O Allah’s angels\nوَزُوَّارَ قَبْرِ ٱبْنِ نَبِيِّ ٱللَّهِ\nWA ZUWWAARA QABRIBNE NABIYYIL LAAHE\nand visitors of the tomb of the son of Allah’s Prophet.\nYou should then walk for ten steps and stop again to repeat the following statement thirty times:\nاَللَّهُ أَكْبَرُ\nALLAAHO AKBARO\nAllah is the Most Great.\nYou should then move towards the tomb from the side of the Imam’s face having your face to be to the face of the Imam and the kiblah direction to be between your shoulders. You should then say the following:\nاَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَا حُجَّةَ ٱللَّهِ وَٱبْنَ حُجَّتِهِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA HUJJATAL LAAHE WABNA HUJJATEHI\nPeace be upon you, O Allah’s Argument (on His creatures) and son of His Argument.\nاَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَا قَتِيلَ ٱللَّهِ وَٱبْنَ قَتِيلِهِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA QATEELAL LAAHE WABNA QATEELEHI\nPeace be upon you, O killed for Allah’s sake and son of the killed for His sake.\nاَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ثَارَ ٱللَّهِ وَٱبْنَ ثَارِهِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA SAARAL LAAHE WABNA SAAREHI\nPeace be upon you, O vengeance of Allah and son of His vengeance.\nاَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وِتْرَ ٱللَّهِ ٱلْمَوْتُورَ فِي ٱلسَّمَاوَاتِ وَٱلأَرْضِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA WITRAL LAAHIL MAWTOORA FIS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE\nPeace be upon you, O he whose blood-claimer is Allah and whose blood is also claimed by the heavens and the earth.\nأَشْهَدُ أَنَّ دَمَكَ سَكَنَ فِي ٱلْخُلْدِ\nASH-HADO ANNA DAMAKA SAKANA FIL KHULDE\nI bear witness that your blood has resided in the Eternity,\nوَٱقْشَعَرَّتْ لَهُ أَظِلَّةُ ٱلْعَرْشِ\nWAQ SHA-A’RRAT LAHU AZILLATUL A’RSHE\nthe shades of the Divine Throne have shivered for it,\nوَبَكَىٰ لَهُ جَمِيعُ ٱلْخَلاَئِقِ\nWA BAKAA LAHU JAMEE-U’L KHALAAA-EQE\nand all creatures have wept for it,\nوَبَكَتْ لَهُ ٱلسَّمَاوَاتُ ٱلسَّبْعُ وَٱلأَرَضُونَ ٱلسَّبْعُ\nWA BAKAT LAHUS SAMAAWAATUS SAB-O’ WAL ARAZOONAS SAB-O’\nincluding the seven heavens, the seven layers of the earth,\nوَمَا فِيهِنَّ وَمَا بَيْنَهُنَّ\nWA MAA FEEHINNA WA MAA BAYNAHUNNA\nwhatever is within them, whatever is between them,\nوَمَنْ يَتَقَلَّبُ فِي ٱلْجَنَّةِ وَٱلنَّارِ مِنْ خَلْقِ رَبِّنَا\nWA MAN-Y YATAQALLABO FIL JANNATE WAN NAARE MIN KHALQE RABBENAA\nall the inhabitants of Paradise and Hellfire from the creatures of our Lord,\nوَمَا يُرَىٰ وَمَا لاََ يُرَىٰ\nWA MAA YORAA WA MAA LAA YORAA\nwhatever can be seen, and whatever cannot be seen.\nأَشْهَدُ أَنَّكَ حُجَّةُ ٱللَّهِ وَٱبْنُ حُجَّتِهِ\nASH-HADO ANNAKA HUJJATUL LAAHE WABNO HUJJATEHI\nI bear witness that you are Allah’s Argument and son of His Argument.\nوَأَشْهَدُ أَنَّكَ قَتِيلُ ٱللَّهِ وَٱبنُ قَتِيلِهِ\nWA ASH-HADO ANNAKA QATEELUL LAAHE WABNO QATEELEHI\nI bear witness that you were killed for Allah’s sake and you are the son of him who was killed for the same.\nوأَشْهَدُ أَنَّكَ ثَارُ ٱللَّهِ وَٱبْنُ ثَارِهِ\nWA ASH-HADO ANNAKA SAARUL LAAHE WABNO SAAREHI\nI bear witness that you are Allah’s vengeance and the son of His vengeance.\nوَأَشْهَدُ أَنَّك وِتْرُ ٱللَّهِ ٱلْمَوْتورُ فِي ٱلسَّمَاوَاتِ وَٱلأَرْضِ\nWA ASH-HADO ANNAKA WITRUL LAAHIL MAWTOORO FIS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE\nI bear witness that Allah is your blood-claimer and your blood is also claimed by the heavens and the earth.\nوَأَشْهَدُ أَنَّكَ قَدْ بَلَّغْتَ وَنَصَحْتَ\nWA ASH-HADO ANNAKA QAD BALLAGHTA WA NASAHTA\nI bear witness that you conveyed (the message), acted sincerely,\nوَوَفَيْتَ وَأَوْفَيْتَ\nWA WAFAYTA WA AWFAYTA\ncarried out (your duties), fulfilled (your pledges),\nوَجَاهَدْتَ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ\nWA JAAHADTA FEE SABEELIL LAAHE\nstrove for Allah’s sake,\nوَمَضَيْتُ لِلَّذِي كُنْتَ عَلَيْهِ شهَيداً وَمُسْتَشْهِداً\nWA MAZAYTA LILLAZEE KUNTA A’LAYHE SHAAHEDANW WA MUSTASH-HEDAN\nyou advanced to that on which you were witness and that which you were asked to witness,\nوَشَاهِداً وَمَشْهُوداً\nWA SHAAHEDANW WA MASH-HOODAN\nand you were observer and you were watched.\nأَنَا عَبْدُ ٱللَّهِ وَمَوْلاَكَ\nANAA A’BDUL LAAHE WA MAWLAAKA\nI am the slave of Allah, the servant of you,\nوَفِي طَاعَتِكَ وَٱلْوَافِدُ إِلَيْكَ\nWA FEE TAA-A’TEKA WAL WAAFEDO ELAYKA\nthe obedient to you, and the visitor of you.\nأَلْتَمِسُ كَمَالَ ٱلْمَنْزِلَةِ عِنْدَ ٱللَّهِ\nALTAMESO KAMAALAL MANZELATE I’NDAL LAAHE\nI seek for a perfect position with Allah,\nوَثَبَاتَ ٱلْقَدَمِ فِي ٱلْهِجْرَةِ إِلَيْكَ\nWA SABAATAL QADAME FIL HIJRATE ELAYKA\nI seek steadfastness through my pilgrimage to you,\nوَٱلسَّبِيلَ ٱلَّذِي لاََ يَخْتَلِجُ دوُنَكَ\nWAS SABEELAL LAZEE LAA YAKHTALEJO DOONAKA\nand I seek the path that cannot be passed without you\nمِنَ ٱلدُّخُولِ فِي كِفَالَتِكَ ٱلَّتِي أُمِرْتَ بِهَا\nMENAD DOKHOOLE FEE KEFAALATEKAL LATEE OMIRTA BEHAA\nso that I will be allowed to enter in your guarantee that you have been ordered to give.\nمَنْ أَرَادَ ٱللَّهَ بَدَأَ بِكُمْ\nMAN ARAADAL LAAHA BADA-A BEKUM\nHe who seeks Allah must begin with you,\nبِكُمْ يُبَيِّنُ ٱللَّهُ ٱلْكَذِبَ\nBEKUM YOBAYYENUL LAAHUL KAZEBA\nbecause only through you has Allah disclosed forgery.\nوَبِكُمْ يُبَاعِدُ ٱللَّهُ ٱلزَّمَانَ ٱلْكَلِبَ\nWA BEKUM YOBAA-E’DUL LAAHUZ ZAMAANAL KALEBA\nThrough you only does Allah throw away difficult days.\nوَبِكُمْ فَتَحَ ٱللَّهُ\nWA BEKUM FATAHAL LAAHO\nFor your sake only has Allah started (creation).\nوَبِكُمْ يَخْتِمُ ٱللَّهُ\nWA BEKUM YAKHTEMUL LAAHO\nWith you only will Allah seal.\nوَبِكُمْ يَمْحُو مَا يَشَاءُ وَيُثْبِتُ\nWA BEKUM YAMHOO MAA YASHAAA-O WA YUSBETO\nThrough you only does He erase whatever He wills and establishes (whatever He wills).\nوبِكُمْ يَفُكُّ ٱلذُّلَّ مِنْ رِقَابِنَا\nWA BEKUM YAFUKKUZ ZULLA MIR REQAABENAA\nThrough you only does He release us from humility.\nوَبِكُمْ يُدْرِكُ ٱللَّهُ تِرَةَ كُلِّ مُؤْمِنٍ يُطْلَبُ بِهَا\nWA BEKUM YUDREKUL LAAHO TERATA KULLE MOAMENIN-Y YUTLABO BEHAA\nThrough you only will Allah avenge every faithful believer.\nوَبِكُمْ تُنْبِتُ ٱلأَرْضُ أَشْجَارَهَا\nWA BEKUM TUNBETUL ARZO ASHJAARAHAA\nThrough you only does the soil grow its trees.\nوَبِكُمْ تُخْرِجُ ٱلأَرْضُ ثِمَارَهَا\nWA BEKUM TUKHREJUL ARZO SEMAARAHAA\nThrough you only does the earth produce its fruits.\nوَبِكُمْ تُنْزِلُ ٱلسَّمَاءُ قَطْرَهَا وَرِزْقَهَا\nWA BEKUM TUNZELUS SAMAAA-O QATRAHAA WA RIZQAHAA\nThrough you only does the sky pour down its drops and sustenance.\nوَبِكُمْ يَكْشِفُ ٱللَّهُ ٱلْكَرْبَ\nWA BEKUM YAKSHEFUL LAAHUL KARBA\nThrough you only does Allah relieve from agonies.\nوَبِكُمْ يُنَزِّلُ ٱللَّهُ ٱلْغَيْثَ\nWA BEKUM YONAZZELUL LAAHUL GHAYSA\nThrough you only does Allah cause the rain to come down.\nوَبِكُمْ تُسَبِّحُ ٱلأَرْضُ ٱلَّتِي تَحْمِلُ أَبْدَانَكُمْ\nWA BEKUM TOSABBEHUL ARZUL LATEE TAHMELO ABDAANAKUM\nThrough you only does the earth that carries your bodies glorify (the Lord)\nوَتَسْتَقِرُّ جِبَالُهَا عَنْ مَرَاسِيهَا\nWA TASTAQIRRO JEBAALOHAA A’LAA MARAASEEHAA\nand are the mountains made firm.\nإِرَادَةُ ٱلرَّبِّ فِي مَقَادِيرِ أُمُورِهِ تَهْبِطُ إِلَيْكُمْ\nERAADATUR RABBE FEE MAQAADEERE OMOOREHI TAHBETO ELAYKUM\nThe will of the Lord regarding the estimations of His affairs come down to you\nوَتَصْدُرُ مِنْ بُيُوتِكُمْ\nWA TASDORO MIN BOYOOTEKUM\nand are issued from your houses.\nوَٱلصَّادِرُ عَمَّا فُصِّلَ مِنْ أَحْكَامِ ٱلْعِبَادِ\nWAS SAADERO A’MMAA FUSSELA MIN AHKAAMIL E’BAADE\nSo do the details of the decrees to the servants.\nلُعِنَتْ أُمَّةٌ قَتَلَتْكُمْ\nLO-E’NAT UMMATUN QATALATKUM\nCursed be the people who killed you.\nوَأُمَّةٌ خَالَفَتْكُمْ\nWA UMMATUN KHAALAFATKUM\nCursed be the people who dissent from you,\nوَأُمَّةٌ جَحَدَتْ وِلاَيَتَكُمْ\nWA UMMATUN JAHADAT WELAAYATAKUM\nthe people who deny your (Divinely commissioned) leadership,\nوَأُمَّةٌ ظَاهَرَتْ عَلَيْكُمْ\nWA UMMATUN ZAAHARAT A’LAYKUM\nthe people who supported each other against you,\nوَأُمَّةٌ شَهِدَتْ وَلَمْ تُسْتَشْهَدْ\nWA UMMATUN SHAHEDAT WA LAM TUSTASH-HAD\nand the people who witnessed you but they shunned being martyred for you.\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ ٱلَّذِي جَعَلَ ٱلنَّارَ مَأْوَاهُمْ\nALHAMDO LILLAAHIL LAZEE JA-A’LAN NAARA MAAWAAHUM\nAll praise be to Allah Who has decided Hellfire to be the dwelling of these peoples.\nوَبِئْسَ وِرْدُ ٱلْوَارِدِينَ\nWA BEASA WIRDUL WAAREDEENA\nWoeful indeed will be the place to which they shall be led\nوَبِئْسَ ٱلْوِرْدُ ٱلْمَوْرُودُ\nWA BEASAL WIRDUL MAWROODO\nand woeful indeed will be the place to which they shall be brought.\nوَٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ ٱلْعَالَمِينَ\nWAL HAMDO LILLAAHE RABBIL A’ALAMEENA\nAll praise be to Allah, the Lord of the worlds.\nYou should then repeat the following words three times:\nوَصَلَّىٰ ٱللَّهُ عَلَيْكَ يَا أَبَا عَبْدِ ٱللَّهِ\nWA SALLAL LAAHO A’LAYKA YAA ABAA A’BDIL LAAHE\nAnd may Allah bless you, O Abu-`Abdullah\nthen you should then repeat the following words three times\nأَنَا إِلَىٰ ٱللَّهِ مِمَّنْ خَالَفَكَ بَريءٌ\nANAA ELAL LAAHE MIMMAN KHAALAFAKA BAREE-UN\nI disavow, in the presence of Allah, all those who dissented you.\nYou should then stand up and direct towards his son, `Ali, who is buried to the side of the Imam’s feet, and say the following words:\nاَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَا بْنَ رَسُولِ ٱللَّهِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YABNA RASOOLIL LAAHE\nPeace be upon you, O son of Allah’s Messenger.\nاَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَا بْنَ أَمِيرِ ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ\nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YABNA AMEERIL MOAMENEENA\nPeace be upon you, O son of the Commander of the Faithful.\nاَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَا بْنَ ٱلْحَسَنِ وَٱلْحُسَيْنِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YABNAL HASANE WAL HOSAYNE\nPeace be upon you, O son of al-Hasan and al-Husayn.\nاَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَا بْنَ خَدِيجَةَ وَفَاطِمَةَ\nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YABNA KHADEEJATA WA FAATEMATA\nPeace be upon you, O son of Khadijah and Fatimah.\nصَلَّىٰ ٱللَّهُ عَلَيْكَ\nSALLAL LAAHO A’LAYKA\nMay Allah bless you.\nصَلّىٰ ٱللَّهُ عَلَيْكَ\nSALLAL LAAHO A’LAYKA\nMay Allah bless you.\nصَلَّىٰ ٱللَّهُ عَلَيْكَ\nSALLAL LAAHO A’LAYKA\nMay Allah bless you.\nلَعَنَ ٱللَّهُ مَنْ قَتَلَكَ\nLA-A’NAL LAAHO MAN QATALAKA\nMay Allah curse those who killed you.\nلَعَنَ ٱللَّهُ مَنْ قَتَلَكَ\nLA-A’NAL LAAHO MAN QATALAKA\nMay Allah curse those who killed you.\nلَعَنَ ٱللَّهُ مَنْ قَتَلَكَ\nLA-A’NAL LAAHO MAN QATALAKA\nMay Allah curse those who killed you.\nأَنَا إِلَىٰ ٱللَّهِ مِنْهُمْ بَريءٌ\nANAA ELAL LAAHE MINHUM BAREE-UN\nI disavow all of them in the presence of Allah.\nYou should then stand up and point to the martyrs with your hand, may Allah be pleased with them, and say the following words:\nاَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكُمْ\nASSALAAMO A’LAYKUM\nPeace be upon you.\nاَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكُمْ\nASSALAAMO A’LAYKUM\nPeace be upon you.\nاَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكُمْ\nASSALAAMO A’LAYKUM\nPeace be upon you.\nفُزْتُمْ وَٱللَّهِ\nFUZTUM WAL LAAHE\nYou, by Allah, have achieved success.\nفُزْتُمْ وَٱللَّهِ\nFUZTUM WAL LAAHE\nYou, by Allah, have achieved success.\nفُزْتُمْ وَٱللَّهِ\nFUZTUM WAL LAAHE\nYou, by Allah, have achieved success.\nفَلَيْتَ أَنِّي مَعَكُمْ فَأَفُوزَ فَوْزاً عَظيماً\nFALAYTA ANNEE MA-A’KUM FA-AFOOZA FAWZAN A’ZEEMAN\nWould that I were with you, then should I achieve a great success.\nYou should then turn around and make the tomb of Abu-`Abdullah in front of you (i.e. stop behind the tomb) and offer a six-unit prayer. Thus, you have accomplished the visitation of Imam al-Husayn’s tomb. You may then leave, if you wish. (Here end the instructive words of Imam al-Sadiq)",
